{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792268366,"nonce":"aOjAJZri7Dxlog9YMmq6/M2AzvU=","title":"RayDE: a full Haxe IDE on ashui's code editor, for ash and rayzor","message":"RayDE, the Rayzor Development Environment: a sibling library beside chimpmonk (its own repo, git-bug and haxelib.json, pinned from chimpmonk the way ashui is; the user creates the repo), giving a full Haxe IDE built on ashui's CodeEditor, tuned for ChimpMonk and ashui code. It supports two Haxe runtimes: ash (the default in-editor runner) and rayzor (../rayzor, a Haxe compiler in Rust with tiered JIT and native/wasm output, not ash-compatible). ChimpMonk uses it as a library: a Code workspace in the editor, Haxe tabs for behaviours, and agent commands over it.\n\n- ashui CodeEditor: value, language, highlighter (CodeHighlighter), line numbers, folding, indent guides, bracket matching, tabs/spaces, readOnly, onInput/onSubmit. No hooks yet for completion popups, diagnostics underlines, hover, gutter markers, caret/selection API, applying edits, or position-to-pixel lookup.\n- Haxe 4.3.6 with the compilation server and its JSON-RPC display protocol. No node and no VS Code in the stack: the language server is ours, in Haxe.\n- ash: --hot-reload in hybrid mode (hl.Api.checkReload), --build/--emit-aot, sampling profiler, GC stats. No debugger protocol (breakpoints, stepping, variables).\n- rayzor: rayzor-lsp (Rust, stdio LSP on lsp-server/lsp-types over rayzor's own compiler) already serves completion, definition, document symbols, signature help, semantic tokens, inlay hints and diagnostics.\n- Icons: ashui will own the icon system (decided); ChimpMonk's SvgIcons macro and its 3232 SVGs move there, asked of the ashui session; RayDE and ChimpMonk both use ashui's.\n\n1. Language (no UI): one LSP client (JSON-RPC 2.0, Content-Length framing, stdio) and a language backend per runtime profile. For rayzor projects: rayzor-lsp. For ash and HashLink projects: our own Haxe language server, written in Haxe and run by ash, on the compiler's JSON-RPC display protocol through a long-lived compilation server (--server-listen / --connect): display/completion, hover, definition, references, signatureHelp, package, diagnostics. On top of it: rename (references + edits), document and workspace symbols, code actions and auto-import, formatting through the haxelib formatter library (pure Haxe). It speaks LSP (JSON-RPC 2.0, Content-Length framing) so the in-editor client and any other LSP client use the same server; the in-editor client may also call it in-process. Document store with versions and incremental sync; project model from .hxml (classpaths, defines, libs), seeded with ChimpMonk's own set (ashui pin, hlwgpu, hlwindow, ash-future/simd). Heavy indexes (symbols, file text for search) live natively in Rust.\n2. Editor (ashui UI): file tabs, file tree (shared with the Project panel), completion popup with docs and auto-import, signature help, hover cards, go to definition and peek, references panel, rename, outline, breadcrumbs, problems panel, quick fixes, format on save, search across files, command palette entries in the existing command center. Needs CodeEditor extension points from ashui (listed above); requested from the ashui session, not patched from here.\n3. Run, per runtime profile. A project names its profile (runtime, language server, build, run, reload). rayzor: its own compile and tiered run, through its CLI. ash: build through the compilation server (haxe --connect), run with ash in hybrid mode with --hot-reload, console with streamed stdout/stderr, stack traces linked to source, stop/restart, recompile-and-reload on save; AOT build (ash --build) for shipping. Debugging needs a debug protocol in ash (breakpoints, step, frames, locals), requested from the ash session.\n4. ChimpMonk and ashui knowledge: HXX inside Haxe (tag completion from ashui component registry, props from their typedefs), tw class completion from ashui's known class list, CSS completion from ashui's supported properties, icon constants with previews, ChimpMonk Behaviour templates, scene and entity names in game.find(...), jump between a behaviour graph node and its generated Haxe.\n5. Agents: MCP commands over the IDE (open, edit, diagnostics, run, reload), so agents get the same view as a person.\n\nP0 Foundations: repo, compilation-server lifecycle, display-protocol client, the LSP surface, document sync, diagnostics shown in CodeEditor; headless protocol checks against the Haxe compiler.\nP1 Editing: completion, signature help, hover, definition, formatting, problems panel, tabs, file tree.\nP2 Navigation and refactoring: references, rename, symbols, outline, search, code actions, auto-import.\nP3 Run: runtime profiles; ash runner (hybrid, hot reload on save, AOT build) and rayzor runner; console and linked stack traces for both.\nP4 ChimpMonk/ashui specifics: HXX, tw classes, CSS, icons, behaviours, scene names.\nP5 Debugging and profiling once ash has a debug protocol; ash sampler and GC stats in the IDE.\n\n- Shared icons move out of chimpmonk first (see the icons decision) so both use one system.\n- Heavy data (file indexes, large buffers, symbol caches) lives natively in Rust arenas, not the Haxe heap.\n- Keystroke-to-paint and completion latency are benchmarked; memory measured with the memory probe.\n- Every feature gets structured diagnostics and agent access, and a chapter with screenshots.\n\n- Name and place: RayDE, a sibling repo the user creates; this plan moves into its tracker then.\n- No node or VS Code; the Haxe-compiler language server is ours, in Haxe; rayzor-lsp serves rayzor.\n- Icons are ashui's.","files":null}]}